@packageDocumentation
The web side of the invented lending library. A Hono app serves readers, an
Express app serves staff, and a typed client talks to the Go lending API.

@module
Books, members and loans: the words that every part of the web side shares.
The Go service owns the data; these types mirror its JSON.

HttpClient speaks HTTP to the Go lending service.

@example
Read one book:
```ts
const client = new HttpClient("http://localhost:8080", fetch);
const book = await client.getBook("b-1");
```

Lends a book. It checks the member's open loans first, as the service
does, so that a refusal costs no request.

@param id - the book
@param member - the member's ID

Reports whether a member may borrow one more book.

Read the Go service's rule in
[lending.go](https://github.com/revslaughter/atlas-carries-us/blob/main/adapters/go/testdata/fixture/internal/service/lending.go).

@param loans - the member's open loans
@returns `true` when the member holds fewer than {@link MAX_LOANS} books
